# SuperCollider engine validation

Before finishing any work on `synth/ambient_engine.scd` or related engine scripts, **run the validator locally** (do not rely on Pi deploy or push to find syntax errors):

```bash
./scripts/validate_ambient_engine.sh
pytest tests/test_ambient_engine_scd.py -q
```

On Linux (or CI), also run:

```bash
./scripts/validate_ambient_engine.sh --sclang
```

## SuperCollider syntax pitfalls (this repo)

- Short-circuit AND: `companionOn and: { ... }` — not `and {`
- Defaults: `msg[1] ?? 120` — not `msg[1] ? msg[1] : 120`
- Close `if(s.booted, { ... });` with `});` — not `};` alone before the keepalive fork
- Never `N.wait` on the main boot path — use `s.sync` and `s.booted` (Pi errors: yield outside Routine)

## Deploy note

Do not use stale `raw.githubusercontent.com/.../main/synth/ambient_engine.scd` on the Pi; use a commit SHA or `recover_pi_from_github.sh`.
